From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:37:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: publish each render's firmware bytes as one
 batch

publish_render wrote about twenty separate pieces (notifier words, both
stages' preludes, Works, microsequences, dependency items and ring
entries) with write_live, each resolving its firmware region in the
region tree and issuing two barriers. On Dota (#177) region lookups and
write_live were 3.6 us per Work.

Add FirmwareSpace::write_batch: destinations are validated first, regions
are looked up again only when a write leaves the previous one, and cache
maintenance (fw_cache_maint=1) and the barriers complete once per batch.
write_live and zero_live are batches of one with unchanged behaviour.
Nothing in the batch is visible to firmware before flush() publishes the
lane head and channel entry behind its own barrier.

publish_render now builds every piece first and writes them together. Its
frame grows from 0x4e0 to 0xaa0 bytes; the pump's deepest chain stays
near 8.6 KiB of the 16 KiB stack.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
